/-!
Bottom cyclic generation and exact middle-raising conversion for the universal level piece.

For every nonnegative triple, `levelFiltration_eq_bottomCyclic_sup_next` identifies the
level filtration term with the semisimple Levi cyclic orbit of the bottom vector plus
the next level. This is proved before imposing current truncation, for every saturated
source module. `universalCoreBottom_cyclic` gives the required cyclicity of the actual
universal level coinvariant.

The proof retains the key and level definitions. The extra reductive Cartan
preserves the bottom semisimple cyclic orbit. Middle raising generates the zero-mode
three-colour words, and independent symmetric mode polynomials are generated by the
selective Cartan currents. Polarization eliminates the two excluded middle colours
modulo the next level, using the same decreasing word measure as the parity proof.

`middleRaising_polynomial_iterated` gives exact arbitrary-mode conversion as a sum over
central-slot choices, with every positional multiplicity retained. The simple-root
error from an adjoint letter vanishes already in the saturated source module.

**Not proved here:** for every `1 ≤ j ≤ c`, that `coreRaisingIdeal a b c j`
is killed by `coreRaisingEvaluation (universalCoreCurrent a b c) a b c
(universalCoreEvaluation a b c) j`. The positional formula is not combined here
with the elementary-complete cancellation for the residual central alphabet, including
arbitrary ideal multiples. No fine-key prefix has been identified with the next level.

`universalCorePresentation_of_raisingWindow` and
`levelTruncationBound_of_coreRank_raisingWindow` have no cyclicity hypothesis.
The latter requires the converted window as well as `TruncatedCoreRankBound`;
a level bound from the core rank bound alone is not asserted.
-/

